config VIDEO_EXYNOS_BECORE
	bool "Google zumapro camera back-end core"
	depends on ARCH_EXYNOS || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on OF
	depends on PM
	depends on VIDEO_DEV
	select MEDIA_CONTROLLER
	select VIDEOBUF2_DMA_CONTIG
	help
	  Bring-up driver for the RGBP, MCFP and YUVP image processors in
	  Google's zumapro (Tensor G4) camera back end.

	  The driver restores the three power-domain dependencies, resets and
	  initializes the processors, and handles their interrupts.  It exposes a
	  fixed P010 capture queue for processed diagnostic frames.  Debugfs can
	  upload one validated RGBP/YUVP command recipe, compressed Bayer input and
	  YUVP statistics grid, then execute one offline frame into a driver-owned
	  output allocation; that upload path is a bring-up oracle, not a userspace
	  camera ABI.

	  This is built-in because removal cannot be aborted if a processor fails
	  to reset before its power domains are switched off.

	  If unsure, say N.
